// What the carter brings to order (Shops/CarterOrders.cs): a tradesman orders from their shop window
// (the Carter tab), paying at once; it's in their workplace's container next morning at six (none with
// the road cut: it waits). "per" of the thing a lot for "price" silver, at most "max" lots a morning;
// "for": the role of the workplace that orders it, "into": the container it's left in there (by def,
// "Chest" unless said); "scarce": not to be had in a shortage. A shop the AI runs keeps itself in by its
// trade's "standingOrders" (trades.json) on the town's account. A player's trade that supplies a thing
// itself (the miner's ore, "supplies") leaves the carter only season.json's suppliedShare of its "max".
// Prices sit near what the shop gets for its work: a lot of ore is a little under a repair's worth a
// blade, a keg a few drinks. What's ordered and not used piles up: ordering well is the trade's.
